# The e-mail MIME corpus is test input, not source. Line endings are part of
# the fixture: the golden messages are CRLF because real messages are, and the
# imported public messages must stay byte-identical to what upstream shipped.
# Without this, a checkout with core.autocrlf on rewrites them and the corpus
# silently stops testing what it says it tests.
src/m_email/test/corpus/**    -text
